  "id": "DrugBank_DB01042 - MONDO_16093",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Melphalan and Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary, as Melphalan is indicated for several germ cell tumors, including Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous and Malignant Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, and it is also indicated for Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary. All these tumor types are associated with Altretamine, which is indicated for Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary. The scores for these paths are consistent, indicating a plausible mechanistic link. The shared indication for Altretamine across different tumor types suggests a possible common pathway or mechanism of action that may be relevant to Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary. The evidence supports the idea that Melphalan may be repurposed for this tumor type, particularly if there is a shared biological mechanism involving the use of Altretamine. However, further investigation is needed to confirm the direct relationship and to understand the underlying mechanisms.",
